<content>
  <section><title>Activity</title>
<para>One technique for solving <term data-schema-version="1.0" data-store="glossary-tooltip">quadratic equation</term>s is called <term data-schema-version="1.0" data-store="glossary-tooltip">completing the square</term>. Here are two examples of how Diego and Mai completed the square to solve the same equation.</para>
<table class="os-raise-wideequaltable">
  <thead>
    <row>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">Diego</entry>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">Mai</entry>
    </row>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <row>
      <entry>\(\begin{aligned} x^{2}+10 x+9 &amp;=0 \\ x^{2}+10 x &amp;=-9 \\ x^{2}+10 x+25 &amp;=-9+25 \\ x^{2}+10 x+25 &amp;=16
        \\ (x+5)^{2} &amp;=16 \\ \sqrt{(x+5)^{2}} &amp;=\sqrt{16} \\ x+5 &amp;=\pm \;4 \\ \\ x+5=4 \text { or } x+5 &amp;=-4
        \\ x=-1 \text { and } x=-9 &amp; \end{aligned}\)</entry>
      <entry>\(\begin{aligned} x^{2}+10 x+9 &amp;=0 \\ x^{2}+10 x+9+16 &amp;=16 \\ x^{2}+10 x+25 &amp;=16 \\ (x+5)^{2} &amp;=16 \\
        \sqrt{(x+5)^{2}} &amp;=\sqrt{16} \\ (x+5) &amp;=\pm \;4 \\ \\ x+5=4 \text { and } x+5=-4 \\ x=-1 \text { or } x=-9
        \end{aligned} \)</entry>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</table>
<br/>
<para>Study the worked examples. Then, try solving these equations by completing the square for questions 1–5.</para>
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
      <item>\(x^2+6x+8=0\)</item>
    </list>
  <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\(\begin{aligned} x^{2}+6 x+8 &amp;=0 \\ x^{2}+6 x &amp;=-8 \\ x^{2}+6 x+9 &amp;=-8+9 \\ (x+3)^{2} &amp;=1 \\ \sqrt{(x+3)^{2}} &amp;=\sqrt{1} \\ x+3 &amp;=\pm \;1 \\ x+3 &amp;=1 \\ x+3 &amp;=-1 \\ \\ x=-4 &amp; \text { and } x=-2 \end{aligned}\)</para>
  <br/>
</solution></exercise>
</example><br/>
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
      <item>\(x^2+12x=13\)</item>
    </list>
  <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\(\begin{aligned} x^{2}+12 x &amp;=13 \\ x^{2}+12 x+36 &amp;=13+36 \\ x^{2}+12 x+36 &amp;=49 \\ (x+6)^{2} &amp;=49 \\ \sqrt{(x+6)^{2}} &amp;=\sqrt{49} \\ x+6 &amp;=\pm \;7 \\ x+6 &amp;=7 \\ x+6 &amp;=-7 \\ \\ x=-13 &amp; \text { and } x=1 \end{aligned}\)</para>
  <br/>
</solution></exercise>
</example><br/>
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
      <item>\(0=x^2−10x+21\)</item>
    </list>
  <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\(\begin{aligned} 0=\; &amp; x^{2}-10 x+21 \\ x^{2}-10 x+21 &amp;=0 \\ x^{2}-10 x &amp;=-21 \\ x^{2}-10 x+25 &amp;=-21+25 \\ x^{2}-10 x+25 &amp;=4 \\ (x-5)^{2} &amp;=4 \\ \sqrt{(x-5)^{2}} &amp;=\sqrt{4} \\ x-5 &amp;=\pm \;2 \\ x-5 &amp;=2 \\ x-5 &amp;=-2 \\ \\ x=3 &amp; \text { and } x=7 \end{aligned}\)</para>
  <br/>
</solution></exercise>
</example><br/>
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
      <item>\(x^2−2x+3=83\)</item>
    </list>
  <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\(\begin{aligned} x^{2}-2 x+3 &amp;=83 \\ x^{2}-2 x &amp;=83-3 \\ x^{2}-2 x &amp;=80 \\ x^{2}-2 x+1 &amp;=80+1 \\ x^{2}-2 x+1 &amp;=81 \\ \sqrt{(x-1)^{2}} &amp;=\sqrt{81} \\ x-1 &amp;=\pm \;9 \\ x-1 &amp;=9 \\ x-1 &amp;=-9 \\ \\ x=-8 &amp; \text { and } x=10 \end{aligned}\)</para>
  <br/>
</solution></exercise>
</example><br/>
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">
      <item>\(x^2+40=14x\)</item>
    </list>
  <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\(\begin{aligned} x^{2}+40 &amp;=14 x \\ x^{2}-14 x+40 &amp;=0 \\ x^{2}-14 x &amp;=-40 \\ x^{2}-14 x+49 &amp;=-40+49 \\ x^{2}-14 x+49 &amp;=9 \\ \sqrt{(x-7)^{2}} &amp;=\sqrt{9} \\ x-7 &amp;=\pm \;3 \\ x-7 &amp;=3 \\ x-7 &amp;=-3 \\ \\ x=4 &amp; \text { and } x=10 \end{aligned}\)</para>
  <br/>
</solution></exercise>
</example><br/>
<br/>
